{"nodes": [{"id": "doc_technical_automation_plan_r3", "label": "R3 \u2014 PR review routine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/skills/pr-review/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reviews only what CI structurally cannot judge (spec conformance, layering, backward-compat, doc freshness, debt); re-checking lint/test/build by eye would waste the review on machine-verified facts."}, {"id": "_claude_skills_pr_review_skill_pr_review", "label": "Skill: pr-review", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/skills/pr-review/SKILL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "claim_the_run_pattern", "label": "Claim the run (clear the queue label first)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/pr-review/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Claim the run", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A routine's GitHub trigger fires on ANY pull_request event while its queue label is present, so posting any later label re-triggers the same routine on the same PR. Removing needs-review / needs-fix before writing any other label closes that self-retrigger door (seen on PR #111, where R4 chained attempt-1\u2192attempt-3\u2192needs-human in a minute from its own label writes)."}, {"id": "moved_head_guard", "label": "Guard against a moved HEAD before labelling a verdict", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/skills/pr-review/SKILL.md", "source_location": "## Guard against a moved HEAD", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "review-status-sync.yml stamps claude/review onto the head SHA at the moment the labeled event fires; a push landing mid-review would get a verdict stamped onto a commit the review never read. needs-review-label.yml's synchronize handler mostly closes the 